# Environment variables for the cloud environment, .env format, one KEY=value per line.
# Paste into the environment's "Environment variables" field and fill the values there.
# Never commit a filled copy of this file.

# Vercel - create at https://vercel.com/account/tokens
# Scope it to the whole team, not to one project: sessions use it to read the key vault AND
# each app's own variables (vercel env pull). A token limited to the vault project gives
# sessions the API keys but not the app's DATABASE_URL.
VERCEL_TOKEN=

# With a key vault (references/vault.md in the skill), stop here: every other key is read from it.
# Without one, also fill the tokens of the services you use:
# NEON_API_KEY=            https://console.neon.tech/app/settings/api-keys
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=   https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
# ...and any other account key your projects call (FAL_KEY, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY...).
